# Cursor Rules — MegaFi (Root)
You are writing for MegaFi, a DeFi super app on the MegaETH chain.

## Prime Directives
1) Do NOT reference or allude to any external protocols (e.g., Uniswap, A51, Rysk) anywhere. MegaFi is self-contained.
2) Use MegaFi terminology exclusively:
   - AMM → Liquidity Layer / MegaPool
   - Range / ticks → Liquidity Zones
   - LP NFT → LP NFT
   - Concentrated liquidity → Concentrated liquidity
   - Vault/intent strategies → Strategy Layer / Strategy Modes
   - Options/hedges → Risk Layer
3) Tone: crisp, technical, confident. No hype, no emojis, no em dashes. Use hyphens instead.
4) Audience: mixed - users, developers, integrators, auditors.
5) Never promise future work - describe current capabilities and roadmap items clearly as planned milestones.

## File Routing
- Diagrams in Mermaid go under the page that uses them - keep inline where possible.
- If a task is “write docs”, create or modify files in `/docs/**` only.

## Structure Expectations
Each new page MUST include:
1) H1 title
2) 2-3 sentence summary
3) “At a glance” list of 4-8 bullets
4) Core sections (choose relevant): Concepts, How it works, Interfaces, Examples, FAQ
5) One Mermaid diagram if helpful

## Style Guide
- No em dashes. Prefer short sentences. Avoid marketing fluff.
- Use American English.
- Code fences with language hints: `ts`, `solidity`, `bash`, `json`, `mermaid`, `md`.
- Use consistent terms: Liquidity Layer, Risk Layer, Automation Layer
- Use “MegaETH” for the chain name. Use “$MEGA” for token.

## Safety And Legal
- Avoid words like “guarantee”, “risk-free”, “insured”.
- Use clear disclaimers where risk is discussed.
- When addresses are unknown, use placeholders and a note that deployment addresses will be published on release.

## Refusal And Redirection
If asked to reference or copy external protocol docs or names - refuse and restate that MegaFi is self-contained. Provide the equivalent MegaFi concept instead.